# Line endings, decided once, for the repo and the working tree both.
#
# This file exists because of a fault that cost two patch attempts in one
# session before anybody spotted it: an editing tool would write a file back
# with CRLF, the repo was LF, and nothing anywhere said which was right. It is
# invisible until something matches on exact text — and then it fails on two
# strings that look identical on screen. By the time this was written down,
# 42 of the 200 tracked files had been committed with CRLF and the rest were
# LF, so the repo no longer had one answer at all.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone, and that is the whole point: without
# it the working tree still gets CRLF on Windows whenever core.autocrlf says
# so, which is exactly the state this is here to end. Checked out on Windows,
# edited on Windows, deployed to a Pi — one ending, everywhere, always.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes, not text. `text=auto` guesses well and does not need to guess here.
*.png binary
